Source: Timo Gurr <tgurr@exherbo.org>
Upstream: No (I'm not sure since we also sed some rootprefix stuff in src_prepare). Needs investigation.
Reason: Fix build on Exherbo

From 154e2d13b68a518e84584500118f312a8ede0c7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo Gurr <tgurr@exherbo.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Jul 2021 12:51:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "meson: Correctly validate that prefix is a child of
 rootprefix"

This reverts commit b2d74870711f859ddc72c5756299d2c2f1659468.
---
 meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 5735cfc7ad..d5d6700999 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -107,7 +107,7 @@ prefixdir = get_option('prefix')
 if not prefixdir.startswith('/')
         error('Prefix is not absolute: "@0@"'.format(prefixdir))
 endif
-if prefixdir != rootprefixdir and rootprefixdir != '/' and not prefixdir.strip('/').startswith(rootprefixdir.strip('/') + '/')
+if prefixdir != rootprefixdir and not prefixdir.startswith(rootprefixdir.strip('/') + '/')
         error('Prefix is not below root prefix (now rootprefix=@0@ prefix=@1@)'.format(
                 rootprefixdir, prefixdir))
 endif
-- 
2.32.0

